Rule of thumb

A simple way to remember where code belongs:

Controller → Does something. (login, signup, logout, create prediction, delete user)
Middleware → Checks something. (Is the user logged in? Is the user an admin?)
Routes → Maps URLs to controllers and middleware.

Your logout function does something (destroys the session), so it's a controller responsibility.


